\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each $q\in [1,4)$, can a positive deterministic c(q) normalize the vertex occupation measure of its critical square-lattice FK Dobrushin interface by $c(q)n^{-d}$, $d=1+\kappa (q)/8$, so that curve and measure converge jointly to one chordal SLE sample and its natural Minkowski-content measure, in ordered curve and weak finite-measure topologies?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each $q\in [1,4)$, can a positive deterministic c(q) normalize the vertex occupation measure of its critical square-lattice FK Dobrushin interface by $c(q)n^{-d}$, $d=1+\kappa (q)/8$, so that curve and measure converge jointly to one chordal SLE sample and its natural Minkowski-content measure, in ordered curve and weak finite-measure topologies?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Natural-Occupation-Measures-for-Critical-Square-Lattice-FK-Interfaces-October-5-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex}.
