\section*{Natural occupation measures of critical FK interfaces}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. For $1\leq q<4$, the rescaled edge-counting measure of the critical square FK interface is claimed to converge with the curve to its SLE Minkowski-content measure.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Row slicing and angular electric spectra determine Coulomb correlations with quantitative remainders. A two-arm outward coupling fixes the single-edge amplitude, and integrated correlation bounds identify the occupation measure and its total mass with one deterministic normalization.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
In the source setup the domain is the fixed unit square with its specified Dobrushin marks. The primary theorem gives the same q\(\in\)[1,4), c(q)n\textasciicircum{}(-d) occupation measure, ordered curve and same-sample Minkowski-content joint limit. This full classification uses that source-fixed domain, not an unstated every-domain extension. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 223 has no Lean scope page in this release. Its selected result is not presented as formalized. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

